From: Danny Lu <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] board: imx8mp: Add Advantech ECU-150v2 target

Adds a build target for the Advantech ECU-150v2, an i.MX8M Plus board derived
from NXP's LPDDR4 EVK. The EVK base is reused because it already selects UART2
(ttymxc1, 0x30890000) as the console, which is what this board uses, and
because it is the base the board's Yocto BSP builds on. Verified on hardware:
SPL runs, DDR training completes at 4000MTS with stock EVK timing, BL31 loads,
and U-Boot reaches its prompt with "Model: Advantech i.MX8MPlus ECU-150v2".

 - arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2.dts: includes imx8mp-evk.dts and adds the
   SMBIOS sysinfo node. pkg/grub/rootfs.cfg matches on manufacturer
   "advantech" / product "imx8mp_ecu150v2" to select the kernel DTB and the
   dom0 console.

 - arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2-u-boot.dtsi: one #include of the EVK's
   equivalent. U-Boot appends <control-dtb-name>-u-boot.dtsi by filename, so a
   board with its own DTB name needs its own file even when the contents are
   identical; without it the control DTB has no binman node and the build stops
   at "BINMAN all".

 - board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/Kconfig, include/configs/imx8mp_evk.h: add
   IMX8MP_ECU150V2_DRAM_4G, which replaces the EVK's 3GB+3GB layout (second
   bank at 0x100000000) with this board's 4GB as two contiguous 2GB banks from
   0x40000000. The weak board_phys_sdram_size() in arch/arm/mach-imx/imx8m/soc.c
   just sums the two PHYS_SDRAM*_SIZE defines, so without this U-Boot reports
   "DRAM: 6 GiB" on a 4GB board and hands the kernel a memory map that runs
   past the end of physical DRAM. Guarded, so the EVK targets are unaffected.

 - configs/imx8mp_ecu150v2_defconfig: the EVK defconfig plus the deltas
   EVE-OS needs, each mirroring the patch or board that does the same here:
     GPT/EFI partition support      <- 0012 (phycore-imx8mp)
     SMBIOS                         <- 0016 (imx8mp_rsb3720a1_6G)
     bootefi handoff to GRUB        <- 0017 (imx8mp_rsb3720a1_6G)
     OP-TEE image into flash.bin    <- 0021 (both)
     U-Boot-side OP-TEE driver off  <- imx8mp_rsb3720a1_6G and phycore-imx8mp,
                                       neither of which enables CONFIG_OPTEE,
                                       CONFIG_TEE or CONFIG_EFI_MM_COMM_TEE
     TPM + EFI TCG2 measured boot   <- 0025 (phycore-imx8mp) does the same for
                                       Pollux, but over SPI; this board's TPM
                                       is on I2C, which needs patch 0028

   That last group matters: the EVK defconfig turns them on, which makes
   bootefi try to reach the StandAloneMM TA (ed32d533-99e6-4209-9cc0-2d72cdd998a7)
   for EFI variable storage. NXP's imx-optee-os build does not carry that TA, so
   on hardware the result is

     Unable to open OP-TEE session (err=-5)
     mm_communicate failed!
     Error: Cannot initialize UEFI sub-system, r = 3

   and U-Boot drops to its prompt instead of launching GRUB. OP-TEE itself is
   still loaded on bl32 for the kernel; U-Boot simply does not talk to it, which
   is exactly how the two existing i.MX8MP boards in this series are configured.

   CONFIG_OPTEE_FIRMWARE_SET stays enabled and is not optional: patches
   0007/0011 make the FIT's ATF blob "bl31-tee.bin" when it is set and
   "bl31.bin" when it is not, and patch 0020 gives it "default y" plus
   "select BINMAN". BINMAN is a promptless bool that a defconfig cannot set, so
   clearing OPTEE_FIRMWARE_SET to reach the "bl31.bin" branch also drops binman
   and therefore flash.bin.

 - Measured boot. The board's TPM (Infineon SLB9673, I2C2 @ 0x2e) is added to
   the control DTB and CONFIG_TPM / CONFIG_TPM2_TIS_I2C / CONFIG_EFI_TCG2_PROTOCOL
   are enabled, so U-Boot extends PCR 0 (EV_S_CRTM_VERSION) and PCR 4 (the
   loaded BOOTAA64.EFI) before bootefi hands off to GRUB.

   This is not optional on EVE. pkg/pillar/evetpm/tpm.go:1247-1251 refuses to
   seal the vault key while either PCR is still all-zero in the SHA-256 bank,
   VaultStatus therefore never reports ConversionComplete, and volumemgr blocks
   forever in wait.WaitForVault (pkg/pillar/cmd/volumemgr/volumemgr.go:253).
   The visible symptom is every app instance sitting in INITIAL with an empty
   Error field, no ContentTreeStatus and no VolumeStatus -- volumemgr never got
   far enough to report anything.

   The I2C TPM2 driver itself does not exist in lf_v2022.04 and is backported
   from upstream in patch 0028, which this patch depends on.

Board-specific U-Boot changes from meta-ecu-150v2 (LPDDR4 timing, board ID
GPIO detection, EEPROM MAC, power sequencing) are NOT included here; they
target U-Boot 2025.04 and still need backporting to lf_v2022.04.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [EVE-OS specific board port]

Signed-off-by: Danny Lu <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
---
diff --color -urN a/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2.dts b/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2.dts
--- a/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2.dts	1970-01-01 08:00:00.000000000 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2.dts	2026-08-31 15:34:01.908016556 +0800
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
+/*
+ * Advantech ECU-150v2 (i.MX8M Plus) — U-Boot control DTB.
+ *
+ * Includes the stock LPDDR4 EVK board file and adds only what EVE-OS needs:
+ * SMBIOS vendor/product strings, which pkg/grub/rootfs.cfg matches on to pick
+ * the kernel DTB and the dom0 console.
+ *
+ * The EVK base already selects UART2 (ttymxc1, 0x30890000), which is the
+ * ECU-150v2 console, so no console override is needed here.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include "imx8mp-evk.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "Advantech i.MX8MPlus ECU-150v2 board";
+	compatible = "advantech,imx8mp-ecu150v2", "fsl,imx8mp-evk", "fsl,imx8mp";
+
+	sysinfo {
+		compatible = "u-boot,sysinfo-smbios";
+
+		smbios {
+			system {
+				manufacturer = "advantech";
+				product = "imx8mp_ecu150v2";
+			};
+
+			baseboard {
+				manufacturer = "advantech";
+				product = "imx8mp_ecu150v2";
+			};
+
+			chassis {
+				manufacturer = "advantech";
+				product = "imx8mp_ecu150v2";
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * TPM 2.0 (Infineon SLB9673) on I2C2 at 0x2e.
+ *
+ * U-Boot needs to reach the TPM so its EFI_TCG2_PROTOCOL can extend PCR 0
+ * (EV_S_CRTM_VERSION, lib/efi_loader/efi_tcg2.c) and PCR 4 (the loaded
+ * BOOTAA64.EFI, via lib/efi_loader/efi_image_loader.c) before bootefi hands
+ * off to GRUB. EVE's vaultmgr refuses to seal the vault key while either of
+ * those is still all-zero in the SHA-256 bank
+ * (pkg/pillar/evetpm/tpm.go:1247-1251); without the seal, VaultStatus never
+ * reports ConversionComplete, volumemgr blocks forever in wait.WaitForVault
+ * (pkg/pillar/cmd/volumemgr/volumemgr.go:253), and every app instance stays
+ * in INITIAL with no error surfaced anywhere.
+ *
+ * Bus and address are taken from the board's Yocto BSP kernel device tree
+ * (meta-ecu-150v2, 0001-Port-ECU-150v2-to-linux-imx-6.12-on-deviceTree.patch),
+ * so U-Boot and Linux address the same chip.
+ *
+ * Only the generic "tcg,tpm-tis-i2c" string is used, deliberately. The BSP
+ * kernel node also claims "infineon,slb9673", but that is wrong: "tpm2 info"
+ * on this board reports
+ *
+ *     tpm@2e v2.0: VendorID 0x104a, DeviceID 0x0003, RevisionID 0x01
+ *
+ * and 0x104a is STMicroelectronics (Infineon would be 0x15d1) -- consistent
+ * with the comment left in the BSP node itself, which mentions st33htpi. The
+ * wrong vendor string is harmless because neither Linux's nor U-Boot's driver
+ * keys any behaviour off it; both bind on the generic TCG string
+ * (drivers/tpm/tpm2_tis_i2c.c of_match, added by patch 0028). It is dropped
+ * here rather than copied so this tree does not repeat the claim.
+ *
+ * Nothing else is needed: imx8mp-evk.dts already has i2c2 enabled with the
+ * same pinmux (I2C2_SCL/I2C2_SDA) that the ECU-150v2 kernel DTS uses.
+ */
+&i2c2 {
+	tpm@2e {
+		compatible = "tcg,tpm-tis-i2c";
+		reg = <0x2e>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+};
diff --color -urN a/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2-u-boot.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2-u-boot.dtsi	1970-01-01 08:00:00.000000000 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-ecu150v2-u-boot.dtsi	2026-08-31 15:49:45.962801588 +0800
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+
+/*
+ * Advantech ECU-150v2 — U-Boot-only device tree additions.
+ *
+ * U-Boot appends <control-dtb-name>-u-boot.dtsi to the control DTB by
+ * filename, so a board with its own DTB name needs its own file here even if
+ * the contents are identical to the base board's. Without it the control DTB
+ * has no "binman" node and the build fails at "BINMAN all" with
+ * "Device tree 'u-boot.dtb' does not have a 'binman' node".
+ *
+ * imx8mp-evk-u-boot.dtsi pulls in imx8mp-u-boot.dtsi, which carries the binman
+ * node that produces flash.bin, plus every u-boot,dm-spl marker the SPL needs.
+ */
+
+#include "imx8mp-evk-u-boot.dtsi"
diff --color -urN a/arch/arm/dts/Makefile b/arch/arm/dts/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm/dts/Makefile	2026-08-31 15:33:49.234459750 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/Makefile	2026-08-31 15:33:49.247510747 +0800
@@ -1292,6 +1292,8 @@
 dtb-y += imx8mp-rsb3720-a1.dtb
 endif
 
+dtb-$(CONFIG_TARGET_IMX8MP_EVK) += imx8mp-ecu150v2.dtb
+
 dtb-$(CONFIG_TARGET_EA_LPC3250DEVKITV2) += lpc3250-ea3250.dtb
 
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QEMU) += qemu-arm.dtb qemu-arm64.dtb
diff --color -urN a/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/Kconfig b/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/Kconfig
--- a/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/Kconfig	2026-08-31 17:54:17.391623116 +0800
+++ b/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/Kconfig	2026-08-31 17:54:17.403738848 +0800
@@ -12,6 +12,16 @@
 config IMX_CONFIG
 	default "board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/imximage-8mp-lpddr4.cfg"
 
+config IMX8MP_ECU150V2_DRAM_4G
+	bool "Advantech ECU-150v2 4GB DRAM layout"
+	default n
+	help
+	  The stock EVK layout in include/configs/imx8mp_evk.h is 3GB + 3GB with
+	  the second bank at 0x100000000. Select this on the Advantech ECU-150v2,
+	  which has 4GB as two contiguous 2GB banks from 0x40000000. Without it
+	  dram_init() reports 6 GiB and the kernel is handed a memory map that
+	  runs past the end of physical DRAM.
+
 source "board/freescale/common/Kconfig"
 
 endif
